  "comments": "In 1992 the ten pence was reduced in size to begin the process of demonetising the larger 10p which, alongside pre-decimal florins, were finally taken out of circulation in 1993.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">1992 dated 10 pence issues</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM# 938, Sp# F3</span> Copper-nickel • 11.3 g • ⌀ 28.5 mm - issued in RM sets only (BU and Proof);<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM# 938b, Sp# F4</span> Copper-nickel • 6.5 g • ⌀ 24.5 mm - issued in RM sets and over 1.4bn struck for circulation.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse die varieties:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Type 1:</span> L, I and A in ELIZABETH point to space between dots<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Type 2:</span> L, I and A in ELIZABETH point directly at dots<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse die varieties:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Type A:</span> 1 in 10 aligned to dot, four tufts under chest, lowest hair of mane detached from back of lion.<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Type B:</span> 1 in 10 aligned between dots, five tufts under chest, lowest hair of mane attached to back of lion.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Edge varieties:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Rounded (wire edge):</span> looking thinner, tapers to a narrow reeding (1992 only);<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Squared (flat edge):</span> wider reeding across full coin thickness;<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5e8ef80420ee9.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5e8ef80420ee9.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br />\r\n© Sjoelund<br /><br />\r\nFor further information and images please visit <a href=\"http://coins-of-the-uk.co.uk\" rel=\"nofollow\">Tony Clayton&#039;s website</a><br />\r\nFollowing are a couple of specific links for the 10p varieties pages:<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.coins-of-the-uk.co.uk/dec10.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">10p die varieties details</a> (scroll down)<br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.coins-of-the-uk.co.uk/pics/dec10.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">10p die varieties pics</a> (scroll down)",
